    "content_schema_version": 1,
    "content": {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Application of integers"
        },
        {
          "type": "subheading",
          "text": "A story about temperature"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The temperature at 7:00 AM was -7 degrees C. By noon it rose by 8 degrees. The change is +8. Add: -7 + 8 = 1. The new temperature is 1 degree C."
        },
        {
          "type": "subheading",
          "text": "Order of operations"
        },
        {
          "type": "numbered_list",
          "items": [
            "Grouping first: ( ), [ ], { }.",
            "Multiply and divide, left to right.",
            "Add and subtract, left to right."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "image_asset": "lesson/lesson-3/operation-order-steps.png",
          "image_alt": "Three steps: grouping, multiply and divide, add and subtract"
        },
        {
          "type": "subheading",
          "text": "Words that mean signs"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Rise, gain, deposit, and up mean positive changes. Fall, loss, withdrawal, and down mean negative changes."
        },
        {
          "type": "subheading",
          "text": "Interpreting the result"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Always include the unit. Say if the result is positive or negative. Explain what it means."
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "image_asset": "lesson/lesson-3/temperature-change.png",
          "image_alt": "Number line showing start at -7 and endpoint at 1"
        },
        {
          "type": "video",
          "video_code": "VID-INTEGER-ORDER-OPERATIONS",
          "segment_start_seconds": 40,
          "segment_end_seconds": 85
        },
        {
          "type": "worked_example",
          "title": "Evaluating a mixed expression",
          "problem": "Evaluate -3 x (-4) + (-18) / 6 - (-5).",
          "steps": [
            "Step 1: Do multiplication and division first, left to right. -3 x (-4) = 12. (-18) / 6 = -3.",
            "Step 2: Rewrite: 12 + (-3) - (-5).",
            "Step 3: Subtract negative = add positive: 12 + (-3) + 5.",
            "Step 4: Add left to right: 12 - 3 = 9, then 9 + 5 = 14."
          ],
          "answer": "14"
        },
        {
          "type": "common_mistake",
          "text": "Adding before dividing is wrong. In -3 x (-4) + (-18) / 6, division goes before addition. Correct order gives 9."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "variant": "cta",
          "text": "Ready to practice. Continue to the regular exercise for 6 questions."
        }
      ],
      "source_text": "Lesson 3 — Application of integers\nSkills: S4 + S6\nObjectives:\n1. Evaluate expressions using order of operations.\n2. Model signed-change situations.\nA story about temperature\nThe temperature at 7:00 AM was -7 degrees C. By noon it rose by 8 degrees.\nThe change is +8. Add: -7 + 8 = 1.\nThe new temperature is 1 degree C.\nOrder of operations\nWhen an expression has more than one operation:\n1. Grouping first: ( ), [ ], { }.\n2. Multiply and divide, left to right.\n3. Add and subtract, left to right.\n[insert figure: lesson3/operation-order-steps]\nWords that mean signs\nRise, gain, deposit, up -> positive.\nFall, loss, withdrawal, down -> negative.\nInterpreting the result\nAlways include the unit. Say if the result is positive or negative. Explain what it means.\n[insert figure: lesson3/temperature-change]\n[insert video: VID-INTEGER-ORDER-OPERATIONS | 0:40-1:25] (optional)\nWorked example\nProblem: Evaluate -3 x (-4) + (-18) / 6 - (-5).\nStep 1: Do multiplication and division first, left to right.\n-3 x (-4) = 12\n(-18) / 6 = -3\nStep 2: Rewrite: 12 + (-3) - (-5).\nStep 3: Subtract negative = add positive: 12 + (-3) + 5.\nStep 4: Add left to right: 12 - 3 = 9, then 9 + 5 = 14.\nAnswer: 14.\nCommon mistake\nAdding before dividing is wrong. In -3 x (-4) + (-18) / 6, division goes before addition. Correct\norder gives 9.\nReady to practice\nContinue to the regular exercise for 6 questions."
    }
  },
